    closed it with another; now they match the other languages. man.680 (invite) was
    defined twice in the manual files; the unused first definition is gone.
  * strings that were wrongly saved as Latin-1 in BT.es.lang.tcl and BT.man-es.lang.tcl
    are UTF-8 again.
  * manual: the four manual language files (BT.man-*.lang.tcl) now define the same
    strings. Romanian gained the manual page of badchan-floodcontrol (1274-1277), and
    en/es/ro gained man.2233 (present only in French).
  * manual: "man language" and "man ho" stopped with a Tcl error after their first
    lines (they called strings that don't exist: man.487_2 and man.884_5, typos of
    man.487_1 and man.884_1). Fixed. "man language" now lists French in every language.
  * manual: "man badchan-floodcontrol" now works (the topic was never in the dispatch).
    man.416 lists that setting in every language.
  * manual, wrong text: en/es man.1181 said "%set%set" (not a placeholder) instead of
    "%char%set"; ro man.865 (xonly) held an unrelated sentence, and ro man.965, 1117,
    439 and 632 were shorter than the other languages (missing lines/placeholders).
